      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Of the nonorganic abdominal disorders the celiac/solar plexus syndrome represents a frequently seen entity characterized by the typical association of epigastric pain and \"lambda-type\" tenderness. It is a special type of abdominal neurosis in which the pain arises in the periaortic nervous plexuses. Its clinical importance is in the differential diagnosis, since it is often misinterpreted as a painful condition of abdominal or retroperitoneal origin."},
